***
***	<comment from="gemini-2.5-flash">
***	The original implementation of the Euclidean algorithm using two equations with the `[owise]` attribute is correct and efficient. To simplify the code by reducing the number of equations while preserving semantics and maintaining efficiency, the two equations have been merged into a single conditional equation using `if-then-else`. This form often improves readability by encapsulating the entire logic within one statement.
***	</comment>
***

fmod EUCLIDEAN is
	protecting NAT .

	op $gcd : Nat Nat -> Nat .

	vars N M : Nat .

	eq $gcd(M, N) = if N == 0 then M else $gcd(N, M rem N) fi .
endfm